  {
    "name": "ft_print_numbers",
    "level": 0,
    "type": "function",
    "subject": {
      "assignment": "ft_print_numbers",
      "files": [
        "ft_print_numbers.c"
      ],
      "allowed": [
        "write"
      ],
      "description": "Write a function that displays all digits in ascending order.\n\nYour function must be declared as follows:\n\nvoid    ft_print_numbers(void);"
    },
    "referenceCode": "/* ************************************************************************** */\n/*                                                                            */\n/*                                                        :::      ::::::::   */\n/*   ft_print_numbers.c                                 :+:      :+:    :+:   */\n/*                                                    +:+ +:+         +:+     */\n/*   By: fwuensch <fwuensch@student.42.fr>          +#+  +:+       +#+        */\n/*                                                +#+#+#+#+#+   +#+           */\n/*   Created: 2017/07/14 11:55:29 by fwuensch          #+#    #+#             */\n/*   Updated: 2017/07/14 11:55:56 by fwuensch         ###   ########.fr       */\n/*                                                                            */\n/* ************************************************************************** */\n\n#include <unistd.h>\n\nvoid    ft_print_numbers(void)\n{\n    char nb;\n\n    nb = '0';\n    while (nb <= '9')\n    {\n        write(1, &nb, 1);\n        nb++;\n    }\n}\n",
    "mainCode": "void    ft_print_numbers(void);\n\nint main(void)\n{\n\tft_print_numbers();\n\treturn(0);\n}\n",
