      "description": "Reproduce the behavior of the function strcpy (man strcpy).\n\nYour function must be declared as follows:\n\nchar    *ft_strcpy(char *s1, char *s2);"
    },
    "referenceCode": "/* ************************************************************************** */\n/*                                                                            */\n/*                                                        :::      ::::::::   */\n/*   ft_strcpy.c                                        :+:      :+:    :+:   */\n/*                                                    +:+ +:+         +:+     */\n/*   By: jcluzet <jo@cluzet.fr>                     +#+  +:+       +#+        */\n/*                                                +#+#+#+#+#+   +#+           */\n/*   Created: 2017/02/26 12:48:30 by angavrel          #+#    #+#             */\n/*   Updated: 2021/06/20 18:15:02 by jcluzet          ###   ########.fr       */\n/*                                                                            */\n/* ************************************************************************** */\n\nchar    *ft_strcpy(char *s1, char *s2)\n{\n\tint i;\n\n\ti = 0;\n\twhile (s2[i])\n\t{\n\t\ts1[i] = s2[i];\n\t\ti++;\n\t}\n\ts1[i] = s2[i];\n\treturn (s1);\n}\n",
    "mainCode": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nchar    *ft_strcpy(char *s1, char *s2);\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv)\n{\n\t(void)argc;\n\tprintf(\"%s\\n\", argv[1]);\n\tft_strcpy(argv[1], argv[2]);\n\tprintf(\"%s\\n\", argv[2]);\n\treturn (0);\n}\n",
